Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 01:40:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10722/11171] Third tokenization data point: the floor is
 inside the distribution, not above it

exp6867 ran the same native_gguf_tokenization_without_inference substrate for
140.79s and came back clean. With exp6863 at 38.4s and exp6866 at 51.7s, the same
class of work now spans at least 38 to 141 seconds.

That corrects yesterday's framing. Calling the 60s floor "too high for tokenization"
was wrong. The floor sits inside a real distribution, so honest work is not flagged
uniformly -- it is flagged arbitrarily, depending where a run lands. exp6866 and
exp6867 differ by a factor of 2.7 doing the same thing, and only one was
quarantined.

The fix changes with it. Lowering the number to clear exp6866 would move the
arbitrary line elsewhere in the same spread. The substrate needs a floor derived
from what a tokenizer load actually costs across runs, not fitted to the one that
failed, or a rule that does not lean on duration at all for work whose cost scales
with corpus size rather than generation length.

Three observations is a small sample and the entry says so. It is enough to show the
threshold is inside the distribution and not enough to choose a replacement.

